{"name":"Candlewick","hex":"#f2ebd3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"candlewick","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The wick of a candle.","The thread used to make the wicks of candles."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/candlewick"}],"entries":[{"title":"Candle wick","blocks":[{"text":"A candle wick or lamp wick is usually made of braided cotton that holds the flame of a candle or oil lamp. A candle wick works by capillary action, conveying (\"wicking\") the fuel to the flame. When the liquid fuel, typically melted candle wax, reaches the flame it then vaporizes and combusts. In other words, the wick brings the liquified wax up into the flame to burn. The candle wick influences how the candle burns. Important characteristics of the wick include diameter, stiffness, fire-resistance, and tethering."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Docht_einer_Kerze_2008-01-18.jpg/330px-Docht_einer_Kerze_2008-01-18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candle_wick","wikidata":"Q849004"},{"title":"Imperial Glass Company","blocks":[{"text":"The Imperial Glass Company is located in Bellaire, Ohio, with a factory located on 29th Street and the offices located on Belmont Street. The factory was razed in 1995 to make room for commercial development and the Belmont Street location was transformed into a museum known as the National Imperial Glass Museum. The building was placed on the National Register on 1983-09-08."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Imperial_glass.jpg/330px-Imperial_glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imperial_Glass_Company","wikidata":"Q6006602"},{"title":"Candlewick (character)","blocks":[{"text":"Candlewick, real name Romeo, and also called Lampwick or Candleflame, is a fictional character who appears in Carlo Collodi's 1883 book The Adventures of Pinocchio."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/30/Lucignolo.jpg/330px-Lucignolo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candlewick_(character)","wikidata":"Q3838768"},{"title":"Candlewick (ward)","blocks":[{"text":"Candlewick is a small ward, one of the 25 ancient wards in the City of London, England."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candlewick_(ward)","wikidata":"Q5032001"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Candle_Wick.jpg/500px-Candle_Wick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Candle_Wick.jpg/500px-Candle_Wick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Candle wick in a candle","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACandle_Wick.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/VINEWICK_CANDLE_WAVEWICK.jpg/500px-VINEWICK_CANDLE_WAVEWICK.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/VINEWICK_CANDLE_WAVEWICK.jpg/1280px-VINEWICK_CANDLE_WAVEWICK.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/VINEWICK_CANDLE_WAVEWICK.jpg/500px-VINEWICK_CANDLE_WAVEWICK.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Flexible wick burning in wax","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVINEWICK_CANDLE_WAVEWICK.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Candle_Factory_and_Shop.jpg/500px-Candle_Factory_and_Shop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Candle_Factory_and_Shop.jpg/500